acvp_ml_kem_768.json: NIST's ACVP test vectors for ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203),
a subset, as bench/std_mlkem_exercise.sh reads them.

Source: https://github.com/usnistgov/ACVP-Server, commit
975de31eb83d87039ec88934fdc47d8c312b892d (2026-08-12), the files
gen-val/json-files/ML-KEM-keyGen-FIPS203/internalProjection.json (sha256
d7a62a2c3476957f56dd8d24f9004ea6776ccfe995ffe71a65bb9506dc9c7b1b) and
gen-val/json-files/ML-KEM-encapDecap-FIPS203/internalProjection.json
(sha256 a556952ce869bb89c3a3196a701dad89647c193a34c86eafb61a9d710d5b810f).

Changed by the iyi project, 2026-10-19: only the ML-KEM-768 groups were
kept; of them the first 5 keyGen cases (tcId 26 to 30) and the first 5
encapsulation cases (tcId 26 to 30), and all 10 cases of decapsulation,
decapsulationKeyCheck and encapsulationKeyCheck; each case keeps the
fields its check reads (keyGen: d, z, ek, dk; encapsulation: ek, m, c, k;
decapsulation: dk, c, k, reason; the key checks: the key, testPassed,
reason), grouped by function rather than in ACVP's testGroups. The gate
fetches both files whole from that commit when the network answers and
checks every ML-KEM-768 case of them as well.

